# Personal config overlays - your machine-specific values (identity, hosts, paths, workspaces,
# projects, ...), layered over the base Unix/config/NAME.conf at read time by Unix/lib/config.sh.
# Written by Initialize-Configuration, the Add-* commands and the macOS Configurator. Foundation
# ships only the generic base, so the overlays are ignored here. A fork that runs several Macs can
# commit its own (git add -f; see docs/unix/fork-model.md) - upstream never tracks them, so
# committing them downstream never conflicts on a merge.
Unix/config/*.local.conf
Unix/config/layouts/*/*.local.conf
Unix/Brewfile.local

# Terminal overrides - a fork's own WezTerm and Ghostty settings, loaded last by the shared configs
# and linked by chezmoi only when they exist (docs/unix/fork-model.md).
WezTerm/wezterm.local.lua
Unix/ghostty/config.local

# The unified backup sink - every real file a Foundation writer replaces (a dotfile a chezmoi link
# displaces, a rewritten config file) is first copied into Backups/Unix/<Category>/<Key>/<timestamp>/,
# bounded by Clear-OldBackups. Kept in the repository so a replaced file is easy to find again, but
# it is your machine's own data (and may hold secrets), so it is never committed. See
# docs/unix/backups.md.
Backups/*
!Backups/.gitkeep

# Run-Tests logs and run artifacts (merged run logs, the measured timings, the impact map).
Unix/tests/Results/

# Session and error logs of the Foundation commands (kept locally for inspection, never committed).
Unix/logs/*
!Unix/logs/Pinned/
Unix/logs/Pinned/*
!Unix/logs/Pinned/.gitkeep
